'''Yambes''' is a [[Torricelli languages|Torricelli language]] of [[Papua New Guinea]] spoken mostly by older adults. There is little data to classify it, and it is therefore left unclassified within Torricelli by Ross (2005).

It is spoken in Yambes village ({{coord|-3.545596|142.746582|type:city_region:PG|name=Yambes 1}}) of [[Dreikikier Rural LLG]], [[East Sepik Province]].<ref name=e25/><ref name="UN-PNG">{{cite web |url=https://data.humdata.org/dataset/village-coordinates-lookup |title=Papua New Guinea Village Coordinates Lookup |author=United Nations in Papua New Guinea |work=Humanitarian Data Exchange |version=1.31.9 |date=2018}}</ref>

